`openConfinedOutputFile` atomically re-verifies only `target.rel` — the *canonical destination*. When the caller's spelling reaches a sensitive file by having a `..` collapse a repository symlink, that symlink is **not on `target.rel`**, so the atomic open cannot see it; it is guarded only by the *static* `refuseTraversedSymlinks`.

