**Why non-blocking:** the feature's real boundary is the static hostile clone, where this is unreachable (the link is present throughout → always refused). The active-swapper variant requires a local process with concurrent write access to the working tree — an adversary who can already `open(".git/config")` directly, so the tool being a confused deputy adds no real capability. It is a robustness asymmetry, not a security-boundary break.

